Subject: [PATCH] route positive uint64 overflow through BIGINT_ERROR
Upstream-Base: simdjson v4.6.4
Upstream-Commit: 1bcf71bd85059ab6574ea1159de9298dcc1212c5

Official v4.6.4 classifies positive 20-digit uint64 overflow as NUMBER_ERROR,
which prevents number_as_string(true) from preserving values such as
18446744073709551616. Route that already-detected overflow through the
existing BIGINT_ERROR path. The repeated hunks are the architecture copies
generated into simdjson's official singleheader source.

diff --git a/simdjson.cpp b/simdjson.cpp
--- a/simdjson.cpp
+++ b/simdjson.cpp
@@ -10888,5 +10888,5 @@
     // - Therefore, if the number is positive and lower than that, it's overflow.
     // - The value we are looking at is less than or equal to INT64_MAX.
     //
-    }  else if (src[0] != uint8_t('1') || i <= uint64_t(INT64_MAX)) { return INVALID_NUMBER(src); }
+    }  else if (src[0] != uint8_t('1') || i <= uint64_t(INT64_MAX)) { return BIGINT_NUMBER(src); }
   }
@@ -17421,5 +17421,5 @@
